  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ \\sqrt{2t+4} \\\\ {t}^{4}-{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{2t+4}$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/d0819fe7e3b82bbf46f6118145903e4dc5640acca4fedf66a734b4d37466e368.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$",
